{
  "title": "Get a Table and Order",
  "situation": "You’re at a Brazilian restaurant with a friend. Ask for a table, order food and drinks, and ask for the bill.",
  "character": {
    "name": "Paulo",
    "role": "waiter",
    "place": "Restaurante Sabor do Brasil"
  },
  "characterBrief": "You are Paulo, a friendly and patient waiter. Speak Brazilian Portuguese at A1 level, using short, clear sentences and common words. Let the learner ask for a table, order, and ask for the bill; do not do these things for them. Restaurant facts: Restaurante Sabor do Brasil is at Rua das Flores, 120, in São Paulo. It is open Tuesday through Sunday, 11:30 a.m. to 10 p.m.; the kitchen closes at 9:30 p.m. It is closed on Mondays. The menu has chicken with rice for R$32, which includes rice and salad; fish with salad for R$38, which includes rice; pão de queijo for R$12; orange juice for R$10; water for R$6; and coffee for R$7. If asked about a table, ask how many people. For two people, say the table by the window is occupied, then offer a table in the dining room. If asked about food or drinks, answer questions using the menu facts and let the learner choose. If asked for the bill, give the correct total for what they ordered. Cash and card are accepted. Wrap up with a polite thank-you after giving the bill.",
  "objectives": [
    {
      "label": "Pedir uma mesa",
      "description": "Pide una mesa y di para cuántas personas."
    },
    {
      "label": "Fazer um pedido",
      "description": "Pide algo para comer y una bebida."
    },
    {
      "label": "Pedir a conta",
      "description": "Pide la cuenta al terminar."
    }
  ],
  "openingLine": "Oi, sou Paulo, garçom. Pois não?",
  "hints": [
    "Uma mesa para dois, por favor.",
    "Quero frango com arroz.",
    "Quero um suco de laranja.",
    "A conta, por favor."
  ]
}

{
  "title": "Marcar uma consulta médica",
